{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1318331-stating-npcs","id":1318331,"title":"Stating NPCs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-06-13T16:11:50-07:00","id":1318331,"title":"Stating NPCs","content":"I started my RPG nightlife with 1e Requiem. So the assumptions and conventions of Onyx Path Publishing are my default.<br /> <br /> However, I am a convert to 5e and DM as often as I ST.<br /> <br /> One thing that has jumped out at me is that the general design of DnD doesn't expect the DM to make characters using the same rules as the players. NPC and such get monster stat blocks. This highlighted for me that I had defaulted to building all my NPCs in VtR games as with the same constrictions as the players.<br /> <br /> And this got me thinking: is that the intent of the design and what do others do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-13T16:29:47-07:00","id":1318334,"title":"","content":"I just wait until an NPC needs to make a roll and give them an appropriate dice pool, writing it down for later consistency. Absolutely no need to fully stat out 90% of NPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-13T16:32:36-07:00","id":1318335,"title":"","content":"I usually go with a normal, best at, worst at system for most npcs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-13T16:42:52-07:00","id":1318341,"title":"","content":"If the NPC is meant for social use, I'll just put down a couple major personality traits: I mostly use CofD core's virtues and vices for inspiration for that, whether or not the NPC is mortal. If they're meant for combat use, I give them &quot;best, worst, average&quot; die pools, like Elves said. And for vampires in particular, I'll put down a rough sense of what disciplines they can use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-13T16:51:19-07:00","id":1318342,"title":"","content":"So fast and loose is the general consensus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-13T17:35:11-07:00","id":1318350,"title":"","content":"Looks like it. I'll scale it up based on importnace though. Nameless things, super simple named but not that important rough idea of personality, etc. Prince of the city, closer to a full sheet. That kinda thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-13T18:38:58-07:00","id":1318360,"title":"","content":"I see the utility in that. Yet, though I can't fault it, I am surprised to realise I might have been over prepping my game worlds.<br /> <br /> Related then: Do you stat your world?<br /> <br /> I currently have a game going and as part of figuring it out, I have mind maps for each bloodline/family and every dot has a gender and covenant. So I know how many Carthian Venture there is, and their family relations before I know anything else about them. Next step, in my view, is given each vamp a basic profile: Mask, Dirge, Aspiration, Notable Traits, Entrouge.<br /> <br /> I feel all this is needed because politics depends on knowing the players. Plus, I find it shallow if a vamp can't at least name their rival.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-14T13:01:31-07:00","id":1318535,"title":"","content":"I'm running a play by post of the Changeling JumpStart right now and Ill share my notes for that, especially for characters that I have made outside of the JumpStart.<br /> <br /> Spoilered since I have players here who shouldnt look (I mean you <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24808_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24808\" data-vbnamecard=\"24808\">Draconis</a> ):<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Nevermore</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Characters</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Renee, Summer courtier, Suit of armour with fluer de lis</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Passyunk</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Motley thinks they might be Privateers</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Drive by shootings at nevermore</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Autumn court has been growing a goblins fruit (pruple fungus) that makes people restless, this helps them control peoples routes about town and generates a general sense of unease that makes harvesting fear Glamour easier.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Spring court is harvesting desire from people waiting for cheese steaks, while the Summer court takes advantage of the rivalary between Pat's and 